    title: "美國財政部制裁與委內瑞拉犯罪組織Tren de Aragua，揭露ATM吐鈔攻擊網路與洗錢手法",
    summary: "美國財政部外國資產控制辦公室（OFAC）已對與委內瑞拉犯罪組織Tren de Aragua（TdA）相關的詐欺網路實施制裁，列入8名個人及2家公司。美國政府指控，該網路主導ATM吐鈔攻擊，並利用加密貨幣進行犯罪所得的洗錢。FBI指出，這類攻擊使用的Ploutus惡意程式具有高度風險，它能透過eXtensions for Financial Services（XFS）軟體層直接控制ATM出鈔，從而繞過正常的銀行授權機制，甚至無需提款卡或客戶帳號。自2020年以來，美國已接獲大量ATM吐鈔攻擊通報，損失金額持續增加，顯示此類犯罪威脅日益嚴重。建議金融機構及ATM服務提供者應提高警覺，加強對軟體層級異常指令的監控，並強化ATM系統的授權與交易驗證機制，以防範惡意程式的入侵。",
    tags: ["OFAC", "Tren de Aragua", "ATM吐鈔攻擊", "Ploutus", "洗錢", "金融犯罪"],
    title_en: "U.S. Treasury Sanctions Venezuelan Crime Syndicate Tren de Aragua, Exposing ATM Skimming and Money Laundering Techniques",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Department of the Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) has imposed sanctions on a fraudulent network linked to the Venezuelan criminal organization Tren de Aragua (TdA), listing 8 individuals and 2 companies. The U.S. government alleges that the network orchestrated ATM skimming attacks and utilized cryptocurrencies for laundering criminal proceeds. The FBI noted that the Ploutus malware used in these attacks poses a high risk, as it can directly control ATM dispensing through the eXtensions for Financial Services (XFS) software layer, thereby bypassing normal banking authorization mechanisms, and even without requiring a debit card or customer account. Since 2020, the U.S. has received numerous reports of ATM skimming attacks, with increasing losses, indicating the growing severity of this criminal threat. Financial institutions and ATM service providers are advised to heighten vigilance, strengthen monitoring of abnormal instructions at the software layer, and reinforce ATM system authorization and transaction verification mechanisms to prevent malware intrusion.",
